BT /F2 10 Tf 54 692 Td (PROBLEM) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 678 Td (Find the maximum sum among all contiguous subarrays of exactly k elements.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 54 658 Td (APPROACH) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 644 Td (Sum the first k values. For each next position, subtract the element leaving the window) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 631 Td (    and add the new element entering it.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 54 611 Td (EXAMPLE) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 597 Td (A = [2,1,5,1,3,2], k=3. Window sums are 8, 7, 9, and 6; the maximum is 9 from [5,1,3].) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 54 577 Td (COMPLEXITY) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 563 Td (Time: O\(n\), because each element enters and leaves at most once. Extra space: O\(1\).) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 54 543 Td (EDGE CASES) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 529 Td (Validate 1 <= k <= n. If array values may be negative, initialize the best value from) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 516 Td (    the first valid window, not zero.) Tj ET
